            "block_content": "3. An employee shall be entitled to use up to ten (10) days per calendar year for necessary preparations and/or legal proceedings related to foster care of DSS children, such as foster care reviews court hearings and MAPS training for pre-adoptive parents. HRD may approve a waiver of the ten (10) day limit if needed for difficult placements. In addition, an employee may use the one day per month of paid leave available to employees for volunteer work under the Commonwealth's School Volunteer or Mentoring programs for the above cited foster care activities.",
